  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 240 PM EDT Monday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Well above normal temperatures with mostly dry \nconditions are expected through Friday. Record breaking highs are \npossible Wednesday. \n\nThe sfc low from the remnants of Isaias continues to slide farther \noffshore today. Behind it, low to mid level clouds clear this \nevening with some cirrus possible overnight into Tue morning.\n\nThe pattern shifts to a warm and dry one for the remainder of the \nworkweek as a ridge aloft builds in from the central CONUS. \nMeanwhile, high pressure at the surface remains centered across the \nnorthern Gulf. Highs warm into the low-mid 80s Tue. Wed will be the \nhottest day of the week with record-breaking highs in the upper 80s \nto around 90F possible (see climate section for more information). A \ncold front pushes into the area on Thu before stalling. This will \nallow for some relief from the heat across northern portions of the \narea where highs around 70F are possible. However, the front will \nlikely not make it across the southern half of the area which means \nhighs in the lower (locally mid) 80s. The greatest uncertainty will \nbe central portions of the FA where temps could vary considerably \ndepending on the exact position of the front. By Fri, a surface low \nmoves into SE Canada which will push the front back north as a warm \nfront across the local area and allow for temps to return back into \nthe mid 80s for most (around 80F north). As such, this week has the \npotential to be one of the hottest weeks in mid October ever. Mostly \ndry conditions are expected to accompany the very warm weather apart \nfrom a low chance for a few isolated showers across northern \nportions of the area Wed evening into early Fri with the front. \nShower and storm chances increase Fri afternoon as a strong cold \nfront approaches with the best chance across the Eastern Shore and \nalong the coast.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Much cooler temperatures arrive this weekend. Frost \nis possible across portions of the area.\n\nA strong cold front pushes through the area late Fri into Fri night. \nMeanwhile, a strong area of high pressure (~1036mb) builds in behind \nit, centering across the region on Sun. At the same time, a trough \nremains over the East Coast. This will allow for much cooler \ntemperature to arrive with highs in the upper 50s north to low-mid \n60s south Sat and Sun and lows in the upper 30s to lower 40s inland \nand mid-upper 40s near the coast Sat and Sun nights (around 50F \nalong the immediate coastline). While exact details will need to be \nironed out in the upcoming week, the potential exists for the first \nfrost of the season across interior portions of the FA either nights \nwith the best chance for frost across the Piedmont. Additionally, it \nwill be breezy Fri into Sat ahead of and behind the cold front with \ngusts up to 30-35 mph possible (strongest winds along the coast). \nThe wind will make it feel even cooler on Sat.",
